# Whole-act partition and binary formation · `guide:membership:graph`

**Section (Membership)** · `sec:membership:area-membership` {{ row('org.peer-network.testing.claim-areas', owner='GRAPH', area='membership').stake }} This first increment implements the records-level partition of (`[ROOT-alg:design:dependency-partition]`), using the closure inputs of (`[ROOT-amend:design:bite-one-closure-inputs]`). It does not turn records validation into family formation or authentication.

**Definition (Dependency partition)** · `def:membership:partition` partition_dependencies takes an immutable BoundaryInputs, whose proposed whole acts, principal closures and fixed pre-epoch history were checked by pn-records. It returns petgraph UnGraph directly, with structural root identities as vertex weights and one least shared act identity per intersection edge, alongside blocks of whole act identities. Vertices follow authoritative root order; each intersecting pair appears once in lexicographic position order. Connected-component unions must cover the proposed identities exactly once before publication. Block members follow authoritative order and blocks follow their first member; blocks may interleave. Shared parents already in history do not join blocks, and removable declared dependencies do not define them. This realizes network-v0.29.2, ``def:graph:dependent-act-set``, within the internal carrier scope. Missing parents, late parents and incomplete paired acts refuse through records before partition. Backend index exhaustion refuses as Capacity, and an inconsistent union refuses as Coverage; allocation failure and an explicit computation budget are not established by these checks.

**Amendment (Partition evidence)** · `amend:membership:partition-evidence` The records-level part of (`[ROOT-verif:design:closure-partition-cases]`) has these witnesses. (`claim:membership:dependency-closures-partition-the-final-act-set`) establishes the scoped block union with empty, overlapping, interleaved, history-parent and dependency-removal fixtures. (`claim:membership:small-dags-preserve-partition-and-indices`) exhausts the 1024 backward-parent relations on five proposals against a naive ancestor/set-merge oracle, with exact least-shared-identity witnesses and deterministic indices in three presentations. (`claim:membership:partition-publication-requires-exact-cover`) refuses omissions, repetitions, foreign members and empty blocks at the publication guard. (`claim:membership:invalid-records-never-reach-partition`) checks exact upstream causes. (`claim:membership:generated-partitions-match-set-oracle`) and (`claim:membership:shared-partitions-retain-complete-results`) exercise recorded properties and six shared cases; pn-verification independently derives components from direct parent incidence. Both tiers observe the same implementation. Common final-marker selection, target/minimum and maximum-duration boundary evidence, earliest host determination and authenticated family formation remain held under (`[ROOT-open:design:claim-evidence]`).

**Implementation remark (Remaining formation)** · `impl:membership:formation-hold` General validate-formation and project-complete-act remain with the rest of (`[ROOT-amend:design:bite-three-step-plan]`); the census and endpoint constraints below freeze the full specification, while executable formation covers Registration and Affinity only. Geometry, graph numeric comparisons and tensor evaluation are not implemented by this partition. No formation-title claim is minted here. The temporary graph is mutable diagnostic output, not a validated input token. Neither petgraph serde bytes nor Debug output enters canonical publication or binding replay comparison under (`[ROOT-proto:design:encoding]`). There is no canonical graph-byte decoder or publication API in this package; the scoped diagnostic binary carrier below requires revalidation after serde decoding.

