**Amendment (Bounded intersection witnesses)** · `amend:membership:single-intersection-witness` Each nonempty closure intersection stores only its least structural act identity. Records retain the complete closures, so a consumer can recover the full intersection without duplicating it in every graph edge. For N roots the graph stores at most N(N-1)/2 edge-weight identities, rather than the cubic identity count of complete intersections on a causal chain; identifier byte lengths, closure storage, scratch allocation and runtime remain separate costs. (`claim:membership:chain-intersections-retain-quadratic-witness-storage`) checks chains of 32, 128 and 256 proposals, their complete block, exact edge count and least witnesses. No allocation or execution budget is inferred from the identity-count bound.

**Section (Formation)** · `sec:formation:area-formation` {{ row('org.peer-network.testing.claim-areas', owner='GRAPH', area='formation').stake }} This increment implements Registration and Affinity under (`[ROOT-alg:design:formation]`), conditional on the declared public authentication verifier; it does not establish title or general family formation.

**Definition (Registration formation)** · `def:formation:registration` project_complete_registration consumes one records-validated act with family Registration, Binary layout, exactly one Binary leg and no variable quantity fields. Its internal endpoint spelling is Named addr/author to Named prof/author, interpreted as the existing Actor/Profile pair; Registration anchors it and mints nothing. RegistrationVerifier must check authentic address interpretation, complete immutable author approval and retained commitments, and author-controlled opening removals. Fixtures establish the callback boundary only, not cryptographic soundness. Approval binds no finalization epoch, position or logical time. A refusal returns no partial projection or graph. Other families, wrong endpoint incidence, absent approval and unauthorized removals refuse explicitly.

