**Algorithm (Registration reconstruction)** · `alg:formation:registration-reconstruction` reconstruct_registrations returns petgraph StableDiGraph directly, with typed GroundedNode weights and RegistrationProjection caches containing the author-local identity and inherited published position and time. It replays the supplied complete Registration history by published (epoch, position), refuses duplicate positions, and inserts each node at first occurrence with Actor before Profile. Each act adds its own binary edge, so parallel Registrations remain distinct. Public removal authorizations are checked by removal position, act identity and opening kind; content and dependency tombstones never remove structural nodes or edges. The caller retains the immutable history and removal evidence. Non-compliant dependency evidence and attached times remain unchanged: this structural projection gives no recurrence, epoch-admission, standing or title verdict under (`[ROOT-open:design:noncompliant-logical-time]`). Cross-epoch paper correspondence remains held under (`[ROOT-open:design:cross-epoch-order]`).

**Amendment (Registration cache evidence)** · `amend:formation:registration-cache-evidence` validate_registration_graph reconstructs against complete public history and checks every live node and edge index, typed weight and endpoint. Arbitrary mutation or deserialization invalidates prior validation; serde graph bytes are diagnostic and never canonical publication or binding replay equality. (`claim:formation:registration-projection-requires-complete-approved-input`) witnesses scoped complete input and verifier refusals. (`claim:formation:registration-reconstruction-retains-parallel-projections`) checks deterministic indices, parallel edges, chronological removal authorization and structural invariance. (`claim:formation:registration-cache-requires-complete-revalidation`) checks a diagnostic round trip, altered and partial graphs, and unrelated live-index stability after backend removal; that backend mutation is not an authorized structural deletion. (`[ROOT-claim:discipline:registration-formation-retains-observed-results]`) compares complete results and success/refusal accounting at disabled, default and trace observation. Shared Registration conformance and recorded properties, broader family formation, tensor evaluation and the bite-wide harness close remain held under (`[ROOT-open:design:claim-evidence]`). No formation-title claim is minted.

**Definition (Endpoint census)** · `def:formation:endpoint-census` The node constructors of network-v0.29.2, ``def:graph:identifier-algebra`` and ``def:graph:node-taxonomy``, are disjoint: addr(a) is Actor, prof(a) is Profile, name(s) is Type, and mint(act) is Content, Item, Chat, Offer, Comment or Message according to its genesis family. Passive means all eight types except Actor. Taggable excludes Actor and Offer; Reviewable includes every passive type. Binary and A sources are the author; each T source is its act's A target. Registration anchors the existing grounded pair; Type names are exact public strings, never normalized or minted. Publish, Owner, Participant, Review, Send and Bid are the genesis-capable families. A self-mint terminal target identifies genesis; ordinary Publish, Owner, Participant, Review and Send may name an existing target, while Bid/T requires a fresh self-mint. Reference mints nothing and uses existing passive endpoints. These are specification constraints for the remaining implementations, not a claim that this increment validates their genesis, mandatory references or endpoint sorts.

**Algorithm (Frozen tensor pipeline)** · `alg:formation:tensor-pipeline` The formation freeze follows network-v0.29.2, ``post:nodes:canonical-tensor-pipeline`` in exactly five stages: assign directional and intensity roles, filling a type-fixed missing role with one; construct the stored 3 by 3 extended slice using ``def:graph:sentiment-slice``; extract the 2 by 2 path view using ``def:graph:path-view-extraction``; augment the stored slice by the temporal vector (1, tau); expose scalar norm(Psi) times sqrt(1 + tau squared), the path matrix and the attribute norm(Psi). The binary mask affects only the stored upper-left bilinear block; signed/absolute marginals and baseline stay active. Full and marginal path coefficients use a + (1-a) times the bleed parameter; half-tier paths use the half floor in the three off-corner entries and one in the polarization corner, without changing the stored slice. Structural identity, endpoint and protocol-reference fields, quantity units, payloads and removal state never become stance coordinates. Boundary damping is applied only at observation. This freezes roles, exclusions and evaluation order, not an executed geometry kernel or a maturity verdict. Both (`[ROOT-open:design:noncompliant-logical-time]`) and (`[ROOT-open:design:cross-epoch-order]`) remain held.

**Definition (Affinity formation)** · `def:formation:affinity` formation::project_complete_act admits Registration through its existing projection checker and Affinity as one Binary Actor-to-Type projection. Affinity's source must be Named addr/author and its target Named name/string. The bounded internal records carrier stores exactly association.numerator, association.denominator, attraction.numerator and attraction.denominator in StructuralBody.quantities, each with unit one and vintage zero; these two fields are representation markers, not economic units or a finalization epoch. Each denominator is positive and each numerator is in its signed denominator interval. Values retain their exact authored integer representation without normalization or rounding. This internal convention is not a canonical encoding, an arbitrary-precision coordinate carrier or executable geometry. Association supplies p_d and attraction p_i under the frozen Epistemic mask and marginal tier. Other quantities, endpoint constructors, layouts and unsupported families refuse. RegistrationVerifier remains the declared public approval/removal boundary for both families; fixture verifiers establish no cryptographic soundness.

**Amendment (Mixed binary formation)** · `amend:formation:affinity-scope` formation::reconstruct and validate_formation share Registration's deterministic insertion, chronological removal authorization and typed cache comparison helpers. One unsupported or invalid act refuses the complete supplied result; no partial mixed-family graph is published. Parallel acts remain distinct, opening removal preserves structural edges, and arbitrary mutation or diagnostic decoding requires full revalidation. (`claim:formation:affinity-requires-typed-complete-coordinates`) checks endpoint constructors and exact bounded coordinate refusals. (`claim:formation:mixed-binary-history-refuses-partial-formation`) checks mixed history, legacy Registration parity, authorization, parallel projections, deterministic indices and cache revalidation. (`[ROOT-claim:discipline:affinity-formation-retains-observed-results]`) compares complete results and accounting across observation modes. The other 17 authored families, general minted-node and protocol-reference validation, shared mixed-family conformance, recorded properties, geometry and title remain held under (`[ROOT-open:design:claim-evidence]`). No formation-title claim is minted.
